thDiscardingTaskGroup(returning:isolation:body:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" method.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Don’t use a task group from outside the task where you created it.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In most cases,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the Swift type system prevents a task group from escaping like that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"because adding a child task to a task group is a mutating operation,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and mutation operations can’t be performed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from a concurrent execution context like a child task.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Refer to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/TaskGroup","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" documentation for detailed discussion of semantics shared between all task groups.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Discarding behavior","anchor":"Discarding-behavior","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A discarding task group eagerly discards and releases its child tasks as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"soon as they complete. This allows for the efficient releasing of memory used","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by those tasks, which are not retained for future ","type":"text"},{"code":"next()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" calls, as would","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be the case with a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/TaskGroup","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Cancellation behavior","anchor":"Cancellation-behavior","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A discarding task group becomes canceled in one of the following ways:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"when ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/DiscardingTaskGroup\/cancelAll()"},{"text":" is invoked on it,","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"when the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Task"},{"text":" running this task group is canceled.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Since a ","type":"text"},{"code":"DiscardingTaskGroup","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a structured concurrency primitive, cancellation is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"automatically propagated through all of its child-tasks (and their child","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tasks).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A canceled task group can still keep adding tasks, however they will start","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"being immediately canceled, and may act accordingly to this. To avoid adding","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"new tasks to an already canceled task group, use ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/DiscardingTaskGroup\/addTaskUnlessCancelled(priority:operation:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rather than the plain ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/DiscardingTaskGroup\/addTask(priority:operation:)"},{"text":" which adds tasks unconditionally.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For information about the language-level concurrency model that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiscardingTaskGroup"},{"type":"text","text":" is part of,"}